<title>JAPAN: Dlr rises vs yen by late Tokyo as rate fears fade.</title>
<headline>Dlr rises vs yen by late Tokyo as rate fears fade.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>0630 GMT	    TRADED HIGH/LOW AS OF 0600 GMT</p>
<p> USD/JPY     114.15/25		114.28-113.05</p>
<p> USD/DEM     1.7261/66		1.7270-1.7240</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The dollar rose against the yen by late afternoon Tokyo on Friday as fears of higher Japanese interest rates receded after industrial output forecasts by MITI showed a pessimistic outlook for June and July.</p>
<p>Short-covering pressure, mainly from U.S. funds, intensified after Japanese institutional investors bought dollars on dips, traders said.</p>
